fact WorkItem(id: "WI-357", description: some(value: "Thread the element type through a destructured Pair pattern over a dispatched spec-op result, so head/splitFirst on a List[Int] types statically as Option[Int] rather than an unbound ?_. Surfaced completing proposal library/002 (List provides Stream, WI-343 branch): List.splitFirst(xs) -> Option[T = Pair[A = T, B = List]] carries the element T in its signature, but a body like 'match splitFirst(xs) case some(pair(h, _)) -> h' leaves h untyped (?_) — the typer does not propagate Pair's A binding to the pattern variable h through the dispatched spec-op result. Runtime is correct (eval_test wi343_list_splitfirst passes); only STATIC element typing is incomplete, so a List consumed as a Stream cannot be relied on at the type level for its element type, and a typed extraction fails to load ('type mismatch in match.rule: expected Int, got ?_'). REF: stdlib/anthill/prelude/list.anthill splitFirst; rustland/anthill-core/src/kb/typing.rs (pattern/Pair element-type inference over Apply/dispatch results)."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-01T11:57:19Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-357", author: "user", content: "HANDOFF (prepared, not started). FAILING: match splitFirst(xs) case some(pair(h, _)) -> h on a List[Int] leaves h as ?_ (type mismatch in match.rule: expected Int, got ?_); runtime is CORRECT (eval passes). REFINED HYPOTHESIS: the pattern machinery (extend_env_from_pattern typing.rs:6537 + build_pattern_subst:6487) ALREADY substitutes the scrutinee type-args into sub-pattern field types, so the gap is UPSTREAM: splitFirst(xs: List) -> Option[T = Pair[A=T, B=List]] (list.anthill:73) has a BARE List param and a free T in the return, so the List[Int] argument never binds T. SMOKE-TEST FIRST (per smoke-test-first pref): try splitFirst(xs: List[T]) -> Option[T = Pair[A=T, B=List[T]]] (mirror Stream stream.anthill:15) so the ARGUMENT binds T -- may be a ~1-line stdlib fix + a typed wi357 test. If not, fix the dispatched spec-op return-type element binding (dispatch_spec_op_cached typing.rs:5769; return-type unify ~2988-3049; thread carrier element via List fact Stream[T=T]). Unblocks WI-343 (WI-356 already DELIVERED). Branch from current main. Full map in memory project_wi357_handoff.", at: "2026-06-01T08:14:35Z")
